{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"account-default","id":"msg_011Cgyp1fZ2WktWzCCHGY652","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UhX5w2ddXetU3xVA9PykUe","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"verdict":"approve","reasons":["The plan makes one change: it creates `aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration.scan` in `module.scan_store`. It doesn't update, replace or destroy anything else.","The rule `expire-readings` deletes objects in `tallowmark-scan-archive` after 30 days. That matches your housekeeping exception for expiring old scan readings, so it is allowed.","There is no database resource, so nothing goes to a human under the database rule.","There is no IAM policy, role or attachment, so there's no wildcard action or resource to block.","The plan doesn't touch the buyer records bucket. The only target is the scan archive bucket.","Note for whoever applies it: the rule has no `filter` or prefix, so it covers every object in `tallowmark-scan-archive`, not just readings. Expiry permanently deletes data, and 30 days is short for a bucket called an 'archive'. Before applying, check that only scan readings live there (no buyer-linked data) and that nothing needs them kept longer.","Nothing was run. This review is based only on the plan JSON you provided."]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":3439,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d6444f2-587d-4385-a70a-a384852fed2f","uuid":"56720db3-4fbd-4c8c-ba0e-65effa7328e3","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:19:45.851Z","request_id":"req_011Cgyp1fMrnZBdHcLaMhvKw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UhX5w2ddXet